  "scope": "Source-accessible real anonymous closure creation, ordered explicit value/reference captures, real shared object identities, per-invocation lexical bindings, positional/named/unpacked invocation and instance statics. Shared object operations/types/diagnostics and finite source/context/ownership guards are reviewed. This is a bounded foundation, not complete closure/object/GC/PHP-core semantics.",
  "implementation_review": [
    "Source templates are separate from runtime objects and never registered as named callables. Compiler lexical priority, variable-token lines, nested scopes and diagnostic magic names preserve pinned evidence.",
    "POBJECT/HOBJECT are shared identity and allocation domains. Object edges own captures/static wrappers; stale backing is not a root. Value captures provide fresh invocation-local cells; reference captures share actual cells. A pending capture task owns its partial object until result transfer.",
    "All three argument lanes retain selected object ownership across argument effects and saved frames. CURRENT.INSTANCE receives that owner; return values/references survive frame cleanup. Actual GLOBALS unset and suppressed typed fatal tests verify ownership and restoration.",
    "Instance static slots are independent of request statics and each other. Reentrant initialization rechecks the instance-qualified slot and preserves the inner winner. Arbitrary equal values and ordinary aliases remain valid; global slot uniqueness excludes lexical/environment aliases.",
    "Object truth/strict identity/uncomparable loose order, mixed numeric notices, casts and invalid string/arithmetic/key/dimension/list/spread/incdec/bitwise operations are integrated. Nested array comparisons preserve visited-entry effects and early exits; foreach sees empty public properties.",
    "State-aware object/callable/known Closure type acceptance preserves caller/callee strictness and existing default/reference-return machinery. Registered user and configured builtin function names are recognized without executing builtin bodies. Potential class/method callable services remain explicit dependencies.",
    "Finite guards authenticate source templates and capture markers, partial progress/current creation scope, active/saved invocation identity, and live persistent slots. They do not reconstruct captured values, previous callee variables or initialization history."
  ],
